      "grammar_point": "should + always + have + noun",
      "sentence": "viewers should always have healthy skepticism",
      "explanation": "Should da consejos o expectativas. Always se coloca después del modal. Have + noun expresa poseer una actitud o estado mental."
    },
    {
      "grammar_point": "there are + relative clause (that)",
      "sentence": "there are some important, if subtle, edits here that remind us there can always be more to the story",
      "explanation": "There are indica existencia. That introduce una relativa que vincula 'edits' con 'remind us'. La estructura 'there can always be more' usa there como sujeto existencial con modal y adverbio."
    }
  ]
}

